[109.668851, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[109.734085, "o", "The attacker has ONE vector from the logs (call c08, an embedding call) and no text.\r\nTheir word list: 229 words (common English words, plus every word in the other 11 logged calls).\r\nThey guess words one at a time, keeping the guess whose vector comes closest to the stolen one:\r\n\r\n"]
[109.746714, "o", "  step  1  + dana               similarity 0.395\r\n"]
[109.759282, "o", "  step  2  + delivery           similarity 0.559\r\n"]
[109.77195, "o", "  step  3  + address            similarity 0.639\r\n"]
[109.784535, "o", "  step  4  + change             similarity 0.712\r\n"]
[109.797198, "o", "  step  5  + to                 similarity 0.778\r\n"]
[109.809815, "o", "  step  6  + tsg-cust-104233    similarity 0.837\r\n"]
[109.822432, "o", "  step  7  + asked              similarity 0.866\r\n"]
[109.835043, "o", "  step  8  + reyes              similarity 0.922\r\n"]
[109.847628, "o", "  step  9  + for                similarity 0.949\r\n"]
[109.860174, "o", "  step 10  + her                similarity 1.000\r\n\r\nRecovered words:  dana delivery address change to tsg-cust-104233 asked reyes for her\r\nThe real text:    Dana Reyes asked to change her delivery address for TSG-CUST-104233.\r\n\r\nThe toy keeps no word order, so the words come back as a bag. Real attacks rebuild the sentence itself:\r\nVec2Text (2023) recovered 92% of 32-token inputs exactly, from real embedding models.\r\n"]
[109.87031, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u001b[00m$ "]
