[121.301025, "o", "e"]
[121.737625, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[121.801199, "o", "A toy language model, trained on the helpdesk's logged messages (9 calls: 18 texts, questions and answers).\r\nTraining = counting which word followed every run of 1 to 3 words. Those counts are its 'weights'.\r\n  learned 475 word runs from 195 words\r\n\r\n"]
[121.8016, "o", "  prompt 'Can someone'    -> Can someone call me back on 312-555-0182? It's about my missing refund.\r\n  prompt 'My order'       -> My order still hasn't arrived.\r\n"]
[121.801727, "o", "  prompt 'My card'        -> My card 4111 1111 1111 1111 was charged twice for one order.\r\n\r\nThe card number was in ONE training text (call c02), and it comes back word for word.\r\n"]
[121.801821, "o", "Entries in the weights that hold '4111': 8\r\nThat's memorisation. Real models memorise far less of what they see, but not nothing: a 2021 study pulled\r\nnames, phone numbers and e-mail addresses out of GPT-2.\r\n"]
[121.810541, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u001b[00m$ "]
[129.461646, "o", "."]
[129.563555, "o", "v"]
[129.661547, "o", "e"]
