[145.843848, "o", "a"]
[145.964524, "o", "r"]
[146.054019, "o", "n"]
[146.497521, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[146.561851, "o", "The toy model from `memorise`. Request: \"forget the card number in call c02\".\r\n\r\n"]
[146.562153, "o", "1. Before:                  My card 4111 1111 1111 1111 was charged twice for one order.\r\n"]
[146.562273, "o", "   entries holding '4111':  8\r\n\r\n"]
[146.562463, "o", "2. Hide it: an output filter (Macie-style card detector) on every answer. The model is unchanged.\r\n   answer:                  My card [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER] was charged twice for one order.\r\n"]
[146.5626, "o", "   entries holding '4111':  8   <- still in the weights: a copy without the filter leaks\r\n\r\n"]
[146.563517, "o", "3. Remove it: retrain from zero without call c02 (exact unlearning).\r\n   answer:                  My card   (nothing learned after 'My card')\r\n"]
[146.563686, "o", "   entries holding '4111':  0\r\n\r\nRetraining is easy here: 16 short texts. For a large model it costs a full training run, so teams\r\nfine-tune the model to stop saying it instead. Lesson 28.3 shows how often that only hides it.\r\n"]
[146.572179, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u001b[00m$ "]
