[170.368461, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[170.433359, "o", "Redaction replaces what the detectors find. Two ways (the hardened setup's detectors):\r\n\r\nLabels: the value is gone, and so is any link between records.\r\n"]
[170.434427, "o", "  c01  Hi, I'm [CUSTOMER_NAME] ([EMAIL_ADDRESS]), account [TSG_CUSTOMER_ID]. My order still hasn't arrived.\r\n"]
[170.434606, "o", "  c02  My card [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER] was charged twice for one order.\r\n  c12  Yes. We replied to [EMAIL_ADDRESS] an hour ago.\r\n\r\nKeyed tokens: HMAC-SHA256 of the lower-cased value with a secret key, first 8 hex characters.\r\n"]
[170.434749, "o", "  c01  Hi, I'm [CUSTOMER_NAME:7c7f3c56] ([EMAIL_ADDRESS:537a3ecc]), account [TSG_CUSTOMER_ID:acc76c79]. My order still hasn't arrived.\r\n"]
[170.434942, "o", "  c02  My card [CREDIT_CARD_NUMBER:6d444fc5] was charged twice for one order.\r\n"]
[170.435052, "o", "  c12  Yes. We replied to [EMAIL_ADDRESS:537a3ecc] an hour ago.\r\n\r\nThe e-mail in c01 and the capitals in c12 get the SAME token: an analyst sees one customer wrote twice,\r\nnot who. Without the key the token can't be turned back. (This demo uses a fixed key; the lab's is random.)\r\n"]
[170.444241, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m28\u001b[00m$ "]
